// 5^(2²⁸) => Generator of the group of size m = 3²·13·29·983·11003·237073·405928799·1670836401704629·13818364434197438864469338081 (m > 2²²⁵)
// This element is used to generate distinct cosets of the subgroup of order N | 2²⁸
//          H := <w>, k·H := k<w>, k²·H := k²<w>, ...
// where w is of order N
//
// Proof of disjointness:
// Recall that two elements x,y belong to the same coset iff (x/y)^N = 1
// Therefore if x,y are such that x = k^i₁·w^j₁, y = k^i₂·w^j₂, with distinct m > i₁,i₂ >= 0 and j₁,j₂ in [N],
// then the condition translates to (k^i₁·w^j₁)^N = (k^i₂·w^j₂)^N, which simplifies to k^(N·(i₁-i₂)) = 1.
// Since 5 generates the multiplicative group, k has order exactly m, so this is only true if N·(i₁-i₂) = 0 mod m,
// which is impossible since m is coprime with N and i₁-i₂ < m.
//
// It is F.k = nqr^(2^s) of ffjavascript's F1Field over r (nqr = 5, s = 28), as Goldilocks_k is F.k over Goldilocks,
// so it is the k of pilcom's getKs, which pil-stark's fflonk used for its connections.
// pilfflonk/tests/std_bn254.rs checks the constants of this file numerically.
const int Bn254_k = 5266228460530200451425464971825753823072228272503274930591399474110020095489;
